      },
      "date": "2026-11-25 07:35:37.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good. Both O2IBLND hooks now match the SOCKLND entry and the kernel table, and fd00:122::169@o2ib parses through libcfs_strnid() and cfs_parse_nidlist() after this change.\n\nOptional, if the patch is refreshed for another reason: consider adding a small sanity-lnet case for this regression. lustre_lnet_debug_nidlist() runs entirely in userspace, so something like `$LNETCTL debug nidlist fd00::1@o2ib fd00::1@o2ib` should exercise both parse paths without IB hardware. No need to re-spin just for this.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
